<section class="mb-(--spacing-md) flex flex-col gap-y-(--spacing-sm)"><h2 class="scroll-mt-(--spacing-md) [--inline-code-border:] [--inline-code-px:var(--spacing-xs)] [--inline-code-aside-ps:none] [--inline-code-mx:0.1em] break-words font-bold text-2xl mb-(--spacing-sm)">Objectives</h2><p class="[display:var(--p-inside-li-display,block)] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]"><code class="text-base [word-break:var(--inline-code-word-break,break-word)] font-medium font-mono bg-[var(--inline-code-bg,var(--bg-base-300))] rounded-md text-[var(--inline-code-text,var(--custom-color-text))] px-(--spacing-xs) py-[0.1em]">PUT</code> and <code class="text-base [word-break:var(--inline-code-word-break,break-word)] font-medium font-mono bg-[var(--inline-code-bg,var(--bg-base-300))] rounded-md text-[var(--inline-code-text,var(--custom-color-text))] px-(--spacing-xs) py-[0.1em]">PATCH</code> deal with <span class="italic me-1">updating</span> an already <span class="italic me-1">existing</span> resource on the backend:</p><ul class="[--p-inside-li-display:contents] [--inline-code-word-break:break-all] [--link-overflow-wrap:break-all] mb-(--spacing-sm) list-disc list-inside flex flex-col gap-y-(--spacing-xs)">
<li><code class="text-base [word-break:var(--inline-code-word-break,break-word)] font-medium font-mono bg-[var(--inline-code-bg,var(--bg-base-300))] rounded-md text-[var(--inline-code-text,var(--custom-color-text))] px-(--spacing-xs) py-[0.1em]">PUT</code> performs a complete <strong class="text-(--custom-color-accent)"><span class="italic me-1">replacing</span></strong> of the resource with the payload, any omitted fields are either <span class="italic me-1">deleted</span> or <span class="italic me-1">reset</span> depending the schema.</li>
<li><code class="text-base [word-break:var(--inline-code-word-break,break-word)] font-medium font-mono bg-[var(--inline-code-bg,var(--bg-base-300))] rounded-md text-[var(--inline-code-text,var(--custom-color-text))] px-(--spacing-xs) py-[0.1em]">PATCH</code> performs a <strong class="text-(--custom-color-accent)"><span class="italic me-1">partial</span></strong> update, any omitted fields are left unchanged.</li>
</ul><p class="[display:var(--p-inside-li-display,block)] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Though <code class="text-base [word-break:var(--inline-code-word-break,break-word)] font-medium font-mono bg-[var(--inline-code-bg,var(--bg-base-300))] rounded-md text-[var(--inline-code-text,var(--custom-color-text))] px-(--spacing-xs) py-[0.1em]">PATCH</code> can perform a complete update making it equivalent to <code class="text-base [word-break:var(--inline-code-word-break,break-word)] font-medium font-mono bg-[var(--inline-code-bg,var(--bg-base-300))] rounded-md text-[var(--inline-code-text,var(--custom-color-text))] px-(--spacing-xs) py-[0.1em]">PUT</code>, the semantic meaning and intent behind those requests still stand.</p></section>
