<section class="mb-(--spacing-md) flex flex-col gap-y-(--spacing-sm)"><h2 class="scroll-mt-(--spacing-md) [--inline-code-border:] [--inline-code-px:var(--spacing-xs)] [--inline-code-aside-ps:none] [--inline-code-mx:0.1em] break-words font-bold text-2xl mb-(--spacing-sm)"><code class="text-base [word-break:var(--inline-code-word-break,break-word)] font-medium font-mono bg-[var(--inline-code-bg,var(--bg-base-300))] rounded-md text-[var(--inline-code-text,var(--custom-color-text))] px-(--spacing-xs) py-[0.1em]">POST</code></h2><p class="[display:var(--p-inside-li-display,block)] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]"><code class="text-base [word-break:var(--inline-code-word-break,break-word)] font-medium font-mono bg-[var(--inline-code-bg,var(--bg-base-300))] rounded-md text-[var(--inline-code-text,var(--custom-color-text))] px-(--spacing-xs) py-[0.1em]">POST</code> is a type of an HTTP request that informs the backend service to create a new resource using the data/payload in the request body.</p><p class="[display:var(--p-inside-li-display,block)] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]"><code class="text-base [word-break:var(--inline-code-word-break,break-word)] font-medium font-mono bg-[var(--inline-code-bg,var(--bg-base-300))] rounded-md text-[var(--inline-code-text,var(--custom-color-text))] px-(--spacing-xs) py-[0.1em]">POST</code> is non-idempotent meaning if I send the same request (with the <span class="italic me-1">same</span> payload) multiple items, it may have multiple side effects. In our code this means the <span class="italic me-1">same</span> user would be pushed <span class="italic me-1">multiple</span> times into our <code class="text-base [word-break:var(--inline-code-word-break,break-word)] font-medium font-mono bg-[var(--inline-code-bg,var(--bg-base-300))] rounded-md text-[var(--inline-code-text,var(--custom-color-text))] px-(--spacing-xs) py-[0.1em]">users</code> database array.</p></section>
